# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 254-261 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 2, 2026-09-26): the camp against the enemy, the evil thing
# widened by the lewd thing, slander and fantasy (254); the night's chance — no minor, day as night, the two camps (255); the sunset and the discharge (256);
# the hand that is a place, the peg on the gear, one peg for both, the south (257); the Shema by the vat, the promise, the Temple Mount's staff and shoe, the
# lewdness that repels the Presence (258); the slave not returned — sold abroad he is free, the resident sojourner, his gates not Jerusalem, oppression by words,
# the gentile fled from idolatry (259); the harlot and the male among Israel not the nations, Tamar's verse (260); the harlot's hire and the dog's price, the
# heifer, the bird, the plates, two not four (261). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(254, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU GO OUT AS A CAMP AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES" (23:10) — WHEN YOU GO OUT, GO OUT IN A CAMP. The head row of piska 254 ({SP_(254, 1, "כשתהא", "יוצא", "הוי", "יוצא", "במחנה")} "when you go out, go out in a camp"): the war camp (20:1\'s daemon, the design\'s (d)) — the full host, no raiding party. Fresh.')
srow(254, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES" — AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES YOU FIGHT. ({SP_(254, 2, "כנגד", "אויביך", "אתה", "נלחם")} "against your enemies you fight"): the war\'s object the enemy, no other. Fresh.')
srow(254, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"KEEP YOURSELF FROM EVERY EVIL THING" — OF CLEAN AND UNCLEAN THINGS AND TITHES? THE TEACHING SAYS "A LEWD THING" (23:15); ONLY LEWDNESS? WHENCE IDOLATRY, BLOODSHED AND CURSING THE NAME? "EVERY EVIL THING"; THEN CLEAN AND UNCLEAN? "A LEWD THING" — AS LEWDNESS IS A DEED FOR WHICH THE CANAANITES WERE EXILED AND WHICH REMOVES THE PRESENCE, SO EVERY SUCH DEED. ({SP_(254, 3, "בטהרות", "ובטמאות", "ובמעשרות")} "of clean things, unclean things and tithes"; {SP_(254, 3, "עבודה", "זרה", "ושפיכת", "דמים", "וקללת", "השם")} "idolatry, bloodshed and cursing the Name"; {SP_(254, 3, "שגלו", "עליו", "כנענים", "ומסלק", "את", "השכינה")} "for which the Canaanites were exiled and which removes the Presence"): THE CLASS OF THE EVIL THING fixed by the prototype of 23:15 — the three cardinal sins in, ritual uncleanness out; the English\'s cross-references to 269 (24:1\'s "unseemly thing") and 258:4. Fresh.')
srow(254, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'WHEN IT SAYS "THING" (DAVAR, ALSO WORD) — ALSO SLANDER. ANOTHER WORD: "KEEP YOURSELF" — TAKE CARE NOT TO MUSE ON TRANSGRESSION AND COME TO AN EMISSION. ({SP_(254, 4, "אף", "על", "לשון", "הרע")} "also slander"; {SP_(254, 4, "שלא", "תהרהר", "בעברה")} "that you not muse on transgression"; {SP_(254, 4, "לידי", "קרי")} "to an emission"): the word\'s homonym (thing and word) the slander\'s seat; the second reading the bridge to 23:11\'s chance — THE ROW THE DUMPS COUNTED AMONG CHAPTER 25\'S (the translator\'s footnote misprints 23:15 and 23:10 as "Dt. 25:15" and "Dt.25:10"; the Hebrew cites chapter 23 alone). Fresh.')
srow(255, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF THERE BE AMONG YOU" (23:11) — AND NOT AMONG OTHERS. The head row of piska 255 ({SP_(255, 1, "ולא", "באחרים")} "and not among others"): the law on Israel\'s camp, not the gentiles\'. Fresh.')
srow(255, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"A MAN" — EXCLUDING A MINOR. ({SP_(255, 2, "פרט", "לקטן")} "excluding a minor"): the age parameter. Fresh.')
srow(255, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO IS NOT CLEAN FROM A CHANCE OF THE NIGHT" — ONLY BY NIGHT? BY DAY WHENCE? "WHO IS NOT CLEAN" — FROM ANY SOURCE; WHY "OF THE NIGHT"? SCRIPTURE SPEAKS OF THE USUAL CASE. ({SP_(255, 3, "קרי", "יום", "מנין")} "an emission by day — whence?"; {SP_(255, 3, "שדבר", "הכתוב", "בהוה")} "Scripture speaks of the usual case"): THE USUAL-CASE RULE — the verse\'s "night" no condition; the compile\'s condition the uncleanness alone. Fresh.')
srow(255, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL GO OUTSIDE THE CAMP" — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(255, 4, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"): the exit commanded. Fresh.')
srow(255, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL NOT COME WITHIN THE CAMP" — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. R. SHIMON: "OUTSIDE THE CAMP" — THE LEVITES\' CAMP; "NOT WITHIN THE CAMP" — THE CAMP OF THE PRESENCE. ({SP_(255, 5, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"; {SP_(255, 5, "זו", "מחנה", "לוי")} "this is the Levites\' camp"; {SP_(255, 5, "זו", "מחנה", "שכינה")} "this is the camp of the Presence"): the pair (positive and negative) and THE TWO CAMPS — the tape\'s Numbers 1-2 layout (the Levites around the Tent) named as the exclusion\'s bounds; the English\'s Pesachim 68a not opened (lean). Fresh.')
srow(256, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TOWARD EVENING HE BATHES IN WATER" (23:12) — THE EMISSION EXEMPTS FROM THE DISCHARGE\'S UNCLEANNESS FOR A DAY. The head row of piska 256 ({SP_(256, 1, "שהקרי", "פוטר", "בזיבה", "מעת", "לעת")} "the emission exempts from the discharge for a day"): Zavim 2:3 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — a discharge within a day of an emission is the emission\'s; a CLOCK parameter of twenty-four hours. Fresh.')
srow(256, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHEN THE SUN SETS" — HIS SUNSET HOLDS HIM FROM ENTERING THE CAMP, HIS DISCHARGE DOES NOT. ({SP_(256, 2, "ביאת", "שמשו", "מעכבתו")} "his sunset holds him back"; {SP_(256, 2, "ואין", "זיבתו", "מעכבתו")} "his discharge does not hold him back"): THE SUNSET the clock of re-entry — the bath by day, the return at the sun\'s going (the design\'s (a) names the sunset a CLOCK parameter at 24:13 too). Fresh.')
srow(257, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"A HAND YOU SHALL HAVE OUTSIDE THE CAMP" (23:13) — "HAND" MEANS ONLY A PLACE: 1 SAMUEL 15:12 "HE SETS HIM UP A HAND", NUMBERS 2:17 "EACH AT HIS HAND BY THEIR BANNERS". The head row of piska 257 ({SP_(257, 1, "אין", "יד", "אלא", "מקום")} "\'hand\' means only a place"): the word\'s sense fixed by two other seats — 1 Samuel 15 the Amalek chapter (25:19\'s receipt ahead) cited for Saul\'s monument; Onkelos writes "a prepared place" (23:13\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(257, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL GO OUT THERE" — AND NOT STANDING. ({SP_(257, 2, "ולא", "בעמידה")} "and not standing"): the going out for the need done sitting. Fresh.')
srow(257, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"A PEG ON YOUR GEAR" (23:14) — "YOUR GEAR" IS ONLY THE PLACE OF YOUR WEAPONS. ({SP_(257, 3, "אין", "אזנך", "אלא", "מקום", "זינך")} "\'your gear\' is only the place of your weapons"): the rare word (azen) glossed by the weapons — Onkelos\'s very word (zinakh, 23:14\'s row): the spine and the translation agree in one Aramaic noun. Fresh.')
srow(257, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU SIT OUTSIDE" — AND NOT SITTING. ({SP_(257, 4, "ולא", "בישיבה")} "and not in sitting"): the Hebrew\'s exclusion (the translator reads it as the standing need) — the peg\'s duty for the one need alone. Fresh.')
srow(257, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"DIG WITH IT, RETURN AND COVER YOUR EXCREMENT" — DIG WITH ONE AND COVER WITH ANOTHER? THE TEACHING SAYS "DIG WITH IT". ({SP_(257, 5, "חופר", "באחת", "ומכסה", "באחת")} "dig with one and cover with one"): one peg for both acts. Fresh.')
srow(257, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: WHENCE THAT A MAN NOT TURN HIS LOINS TOWARD THE SOUTH? "RETURN AND COVER". ({SP_(257, 6, "הופך", "מתניו", "כלפי", "דרום")} "turn his loins toward the south"): the sanctuary\'s direction (from the Galilee) honored — a PLACE parameter the Tosefta names (the English\'s Megillah 4:26). Fresh.')
srow(258, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD WALKS IN THE MIDST OF YOUR CAMP" (23:15) — HENCE: A MAN SHALL NOT RECITE THE SHEMA BESIDE THE LAUNDERERS\' VAT, NOR ENTER A BATHHOUSE OR TANNERY WITH SCROLLS AND PHYLACTERIES IN HIS HAND. The head row of piska 258 — READ BEFORE at chapter 6\'s ledger (the Shema\'s recital), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(258, 1, "לא", "יקרא", "אדם", "את", "שמע")} "a man shall not recite the Shema"; {SP_(258, 1, "משרה", "של", "כובסים")} "the launderers\' soaking vat"; {SP_(258, 1, "וספרים", "ותפלין", "בידו")} "scrolls and phylacteries in his hand"): the camp\'s holiness carried to the recital and the holy objects — Berakhot 3:5 the English\'s "cf."; the Presence walking a heaven entry (the design\'s (d)). Reread.')
srow(258, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO SAVE YOU AND GIVE YOUR ENEMIES BEFORE YOU" — IF YOU DID ALL THAT IS SAID IN THE MATTER, IN THE END HE SAVES YOU. ({SP_(258, 2, "אם", "עשית", "כל", "האמור", "בענין")} "if you did all that is said in the matter"): the promise conditioned on the camp\'s laws — 200:3\'s trope (the English). Fresh.')
srow(258, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOUR CAMP SHALL BE HOLY" — SANCTIFY IT; HENCE: A MAN SHALL NOT ENTER THE TEMPLE MOUNT WITH HIS STAFF, HIS SHOE, HIS MONEY-BELT OR THE DUST ON HIS FEET. ({SP_(258, 3, "קדשהו")} "sanctify it"; {SP_(258, 3, "להר", "הבית", "במקלו", "ובמנעלו", "ובאפנדתו")} "to the Temple Mount with his staff, his shoe and his money-belt"): Berakhot 9:5 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the camp of the Presence (255:5) is the Mount; the verse\'s "shall be" read as "make it". Fresh.')
srow(258, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HE SEE NO UNSEEMLY THING IN YOU AND TURN FROM YOU" — LEWDNESS REMOVES THE PRESENCE. ({SP_(258, 4, "שעריות", "מסלקות", "את", "השכינה")} "lewdness removes the Presence"): 254:3\'s prototype stated for itself — the effect on the heaven ledger; Onkelos\'s "His Memra turn from doing you good" (23:15\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(259, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"DELIVER NOT A SLAVE TO HIS MASTER" (23:16) — HENCE: HE WHO SELLS HIS SLAVE TO GENTILES OR ABROAD — THE SLAVE GOES OUT FREE. The head row of piska 259 ({SP_(259, 1, "המוכר", "עבדו", "לגוים")} "he who sells his slave to gentiles"; {SP_(259, 1, "או", "לחוצה", "לארץ")} "or abroad"; {SP_(259, 1, "יצא", "בן", "חורים")} "goes out a free man"): THE SLAVE FREED by the sale itself — an effect on his status (the design\'s (e)); the Hebrew cites no tractate here. Fresh.')
srow(259, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO ESCAPES TO YOU FROM HIS MASTER" — TO INCLUDE THE RESIDENT SOJOURNER. ({SP_(259, 2, "לרבות", "גר", "תושב")} "to include the resident sojourner"): the class widened. Fresh.')
srow(259, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL DWELL WITH YOU" (23:17) — NOT IN A CITY BY HIMSELF; "IN YOUR MIDST" — NOT ON THE FRONTIER. ({SP_(259, 3, "ולא", "בעיר", "עצמו")} "and not in a city by himself"; {SP_(259, 3, "ולא", "בספר")} "and not on the frontier"): two PLACE parameters — among Israel, inland. Fresh.')
srow(259, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE PLACE HE CHOOSES" — WHERE HIS LIVELIHOOD COMES OUT. ({SP_(259, 4, "שפרנסתו", "יוצאה")} "where his livelihood comes out"): his choice by his trade. Fresh.')
srow(259, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ONE OF YOUR GATES" — IN YOUR GATES AND NOT IN JERUSALEM; "IN ONE OF YOUR GATES" — THAT HE NOT WANDER FROM CITY TO CITY. READ BEFORE at chapters 19-21\'s ledger (the rebellious son\'s "anywhere but Jerusalem" — the English\'s Tosefta note), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(259, 5, "בשעריך", "ולא", "בירושלם")} "in your gates and not in Jerusalem"; {SP_(259, 5, "שלא", "יהא", "גולה", "מעיר", "לעיר")} "that he not wander from city to city"): Jerusalem no tribe\'s inheritance, so no gate of his; the parser\'s [1] "one of your gates" read as ONE city — a status fixed to a place. Reread.')
srow(259, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHERE IT IS GOOD FOR HIM" — FROM A BAD DWELLING TO A FINE ONE. ({SP_(259, 6, "מנוה", "הרע", "לנוה", "היפה")} "from a bad dwelling to a fine one"): the good his betterment — 251:2\'s foil. Fresh.')
srow(259, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"OPPRESS HIM NOT" — THIS IS OPPRESSION BY WORDS. ({SP_(259, 7, "זו", "הונאת", "דברים")} "this is oppression by words"): Bava Metzia 4:10\'s verbal wrong (the English\'s "cf." — "remember your fathers\' deeds" forbidden) — the effect a prohibition on speech. Fresh.')
srow(259, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "DELIVER NOT A SLAVE TO HIS MASTER" — SCRIPTURE SPEAKS OF A GENTILE WHO FLED FROM IDOLATRY. ({SP_(259, 8, "בגוי", "שנצל", "מעבודה", "זרה")} "of a gentile who escaped from idolatry"): the second reading — the refugee from the cult; ONKELOS TAKES THIS ONE ("a slave of the nations", 23:16\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(260, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO HARLOT OF ISRAEL\'S DAUGHTERS" (23:18) — YOU ARE NOT WARNED ABOUT HER AMONG THE NATIONS; "NO MALE OF ISRAEL\'S SONS" — NOT WARNED ABOUT HIM AMONG THE NATIONS. THE TWO ARGUMENTS (THE HARLOT THE LIGHTER, THE MALE THE GRAVER) AND THEIR REVERSE; WHY SAY "MALE"? IT NEEDED SAYING — ELSE THE LIGHTER WOULD HAVE TAUGHT THE GRAVER AMONG THE NATIONS. The head row of piska 260 ({SP_(260, 1, "אי", "אתה", "מזהר", "עליה", "באמות")} "you are not warned about her among the nations"; {SP_(260, 1, "קדשה", "קלה")} "the harlot the lighter"; {SP_(260, 1, "קדש", "חמור")} "the male the graver"; {SP_(260, 1, "צריך", "לאמרו")} "it needed saying"): THE SCOPE Israel alone, both sexes — the redundancy of "male" the block on an a fortiori; Onkelos reads the verse as marriage with slaves (23:18\'s row), the spine as harlotry. Fresh.')
srow(260, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "NO HARLOT" — A WARNING TO THE UNATTACHED WOMAN, AS GENESIS 38:21 "THERE WAS NO HARLOT HERE". ({SP_(260, 2, "זו", "אזהרה", "למפנה")} "this is a warning to the unattached woman (mufnah)"; {SP_(260, 2, "לא", "היתה", "בזה", "קדשה")} "there was no harlot here"): TAMAR\'S VERSE — the tape\'s Genesis 38 (Judah\'s levirate, 25:5\'s readback) cited for the harlot\'s name; the rare-text row (the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(261, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BRING NOT A HARLOT\'S HIRE" (23:19) — ONLY A HARLOT\'S? THE HIRE OF EVERY FORBIDDEN UNION — WHENCE? "HIRE" OF ANY. WHAT IS A HARLOT\'S HIRE? "HERE IS THIS LAMB AS YOUR HIRE" — EVEN A HUNDRED, ALL FORBIDDEN; "HERE IS A LAMB, LET YOUR SLAVE-GIRL LIE WITH MY SLAVE" — RABBI: NO HIRE; THE SAGES: A HIRE. The head row of piska 261 ({SP_(261, 1, "אתנן", "כל", "העריות", "מנין")} "the hire of all the forbidden unions — whence?"; {SP_(261, 1, "הילך", "טלה", "זה", "בשכרך")} "here is this lamb as your hire"; {SP_(261, 1, "אפלו", "מאה", "כלם", "אסורים")} "even a hundred, all forbidden"; {SP_(261, 1, "ותלין", "שפחתך", "אצל", "עבדי")} "and let your slave-girl lie with my slave"): Temurah 6:2 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the hire\'s class and the disputed case; the design\'s DV23-03. Fresh.')
srow(261, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"OR A DOG\'S PRICE" — WHAT IS IT? "HERE IS THIS LAMB IN EXCHANGE FOR THIS DOG"; EVEN IF HE ONLY WALKED IT THROUGH THE COURT, LIABLE? "ABOMINATION" HERE AND "ABOMINATION" THERE (17:1) — AS THERE FOR A SACRIFICE, SO HERE FOR A SACRIFICE. READ BEFORE at chapters 17-18\'s ledger (17:1\'s blemished offering), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(261, 2, "איזהו", "מחיר", "כלב")} "what is a dog\'s price?"; {SP_(261, 2, "תחת", "כלב", "זה")} "in exchange for this dog"; {SP_(261, 2, "נאמר", "כאן", "תועבה", "ונאמר", "להלן", "תועבה")} "\'abomination\' is said here and said there"; {SP_(261, 2, "לשם", "זבח")} "as a sacrifice"): THE ABOMINATION FORMULA\'S TWO SEATS (find 5) joined by a verbal analogy — the bar on the altar\'s offering, not the court\'s floor; Temurah 6:3. Reread.')
srow(261, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"A VOW" — EXCLUDING A THING ALREADY VOWED; "ANY VOW" — TO INCLUDE A HIGH PLACE. ({SP_(261, 3, "פרט", "לדבר", "הנדור")} "excluding a thing already vowed"; {SP_(261, 3, "לרבות", "במה")} "to include a high place (bamah)"): the hire must precede the vow; the private altar\'s era in (the Tosefta\'s rows the English names). Fresh.')
srow(261, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE HOUSE OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" — EXCLUDING THE PURIFICATION HEIFER, WHICH COMES NOT TO THE HOUSE: R. ELIEZER; THE SAGES: TO INCLUDE THE GOLD PLATES. ({SP_(261, 4, "פרט", "לפרת", "חטאת")} "excluding the purification heifer"; {SP_(261, 4, "שאינה", "באה", "לבית")} "which does not come to the House"; {SP_(261, 4, "להביא", "את", "הרקועים")} "to include the gold plates"): Numbers 19\'s heifer (burned outside) disputed; the sanctuary\'s plating in — Onkelos\'s "house of the sanctuary" (23:19\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(261, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ANY VOW" — TO INCLUDE THE BIRD: CONSECRATED BEASTS, WHICH A BLEMISH DISQUALIFIES, TAKE NO HIRE OR PRICE, SO THE BIRD, WHICH NO BLEMISH DISQUALIFIES? "ANY VOW" INCLUDES IT. EVEN THE HIRE OF HER TIME FORBIDDEN? "FOR BOTH OF THEM ARE AN ABOMINATION" — TWO AND NOT FOUR. ({SP_(261, 5, "להביא", "את", "העוף")} "to include the bird"; {SP_(261, 5, "שהמום", "פוסל", "בהם")} "which a blemish disqualifies"; {SP_(261, 5, "שכר", "פקעתה")} "the hire of her time"; {SP_(261, 5, "שנים", "ולא", "ארבעה")} "two and not four"): Temurah 6:4 the answer sheet\'s row; THE PARSER\'S [2] "both of them" (starred) read as a bound — the hire and the price alone, not the harlot\'s price or the dog\'s hire. Fresh.')
srow(261, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEM" — AND NOT THEIR OFFSPRING NOR THEIR EXCHANGES. ({SP_(261, 6, "ולא", "ולדותיהם", "ולא", "חליפיהם")} "not their offspring nor their exchanges"): the bar on the animals themselves — Temurah 6:3\'s close. Fresh.')
